GSSG — Research-Only (Non-Commercial) License
=============================================

Copyright (C) 2024-2026, the GSSG authors. All rights reserved.

GSSG ("the Software") is a semantic-aware 3D Gaussian Splatting SLAM
system built on top of RTG-SLAM (https://github.com/MisEty/RTG-SLAM), which is
itself derived from the 3D Gaussian Splatting software developed by Inria and the
Max Planck Institut fuer Informatik (MPII). Portions of the Software are
distributed under, and remain subject to, the Inria Gaussian-Splatting License
and the licenses of the other third-party components listed in
docs/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md. This top-level license governs the first-party code in
this repository and DOES NOT relax any restriction imposed by those upstream
licenses.

Because the Software incorporates and depends on third-party components licensed
for non-commercial research use only — most notably the Inria/MPII
Gaussian-Splatting rasterizer in thirdparty/gaussian-rasterizer (together with
simple-knn and cuda-utils), the Apple MobileCLIP model weights, and the AGPL-3.0
FastSAM/Ultralytics backend — the Software as a whole is made available for
NON-COMMERCIAL, ACADEMIC, AND RESEARCH USE ONLY.

